{%- comment -%}
  THE NON SOMM ORB — a persistent way in.

  The Somm is the distinctive thing about this store and, until now, a customer
  who scrolled past the hero could not reach it again without scrolling back.
  This keeps it one tap away from anywhere on the page.

  WHY IT SAYS WHAT IT IS. The desktop orb has always been a blurred light with
  no label — beautiful, and unreadable as a control. So this carries a short
  visible label, "Ask NON Somm", which collapses to the mark alone once someone
  has used it. The mark stays; the explanation is only needed once.

  WHAT IT MUST NOT DO. It must not compete with Add to cart, and it must not
  sit on top of anything. Its position is driven by --non-orb-bottom, which the
  sticky purchase bar raises when it appears and the safe-area inset raises
  again on a notched phone. Every layer that takes over the screen — the cart
  drawer, the Somm sheet itself, the lotto, the menu — hides it, because two
  things asking for attention is one too many.

  Rendered from theme.liquid on the templates that have a Somm to open.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  TWO STATES, ONE COMPONENT.

    integrated — large, art-directed, inside the page composition. It is the
                 Somm's presence in the NON world, not a widget parked in a
                 corner. Rendered by the hero and by the PDP's "still
                 deciding?" band, beside the words that explain it.

    compact    — small and persistent, lower-right, and only ever visible once
                 the integrated one has left the screen. It is a way back to a
                 conversation, not an advertisement for one.

  Never both at once. somm-orb.js owns that, gating on scroll position.

  `orb_variant` picks which. Everything else — the context payload, the
  accessible name, the shared sheet it opens — is identical, because they are
  the same control in two sizes.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign variant = orb_variant | default: 'compact' -%}

<button
  type="button"
  class="non-orb non-orb--{{ variant }}"
  {% if variant == 'integrated' %}data-non-orb-integrated{% else %}data-non-orb{% endif %}
  data-non-somm-open
  data-somm-surface="{{ orb_surface | default: 'floating_orb' }}"
  data-somm-context="{{ orb_context | default: 'home' }}"
  {%- comment -%}
    On a product page the orb carries the same payload the inline entry does,
    so a conversation opened from it already knows which bottle is on screen.
    product.js keeps the variant in step when the pack size changes; it selects
    on [data-non-somm-pdp], which is why that marker is here too.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if orb_context == 'product' and product != blank %}
    data-non-somm-pdp
    data-somm-code="{{ orb_code }}"
    data-somm-product="{{ product.id }}"
    data-somm-variant="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}"
    data-somm-product-title="{{ product.title | escape }}"
    data-somm-product-price="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.price | money }}"
    data-somm-product-available="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.available }}"
  {%- endif %}
  aria-label="{{ 'sections.somm.orb_label' | t }}"
  {%- comment -%}
    The compact orb starts hidden and is revealed by script once the integrated
    one has gone. The integrated orb is part of the page and is present from
    first paint — hiding it would be hiding the composition.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% if variant != 'integrated' %}hidden{% endif %}>
  {%- comment -%}
    The mark is the full stop from "NON." — the same mark the working state
    uses. aria-hidden because the button already has an accessible name; a
    screen reader does not need to be told there is a dot.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The glow is its own element rather than a pseudo-element on the button.
    Two reasons: it can breathe on its own transform without the button's
    focus ring or hit area moving with it, and it keeps this component clear
    of preflight check 6, which owns the position of the ORIGINAL orb
    (.non-somm::before) and exists because that one moved every time anyone
    touched the stylesheet.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <span class="non-orb__glow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  {%- if variant == 'integrated' -%}
    {%- if orb_caption != blank -%}
      <span class="non-orb__caption" aria-hidden="true">{{ orb_caption }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- else -%}
    <span class="non-orb__label" data-non-orb-label>{{ 'sections.somm.orb_label' | t }}</span>
  {%- endif -%}
</button>
